note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
note aesgcm.om: AES (FIPS 197) and AES-GCM (NIST SP 800-38D) for om/tls, module code AG.
note Library unit: no om2 line, no fn main, no mutable globals. The build writes `om2`, the om/tls
note library files, then a program.
note
note API (return codes: 0 ok, 1 authentication failure (open only), 2 bad parameters):
note   aes_gcm_seal ctl kia buf / aes_gcm_open ctl kia buf
note     kia = key || iv || aad. ctl = klen + 256 * tlen + 65536 * ivlen:
note       bits 0..7 klen (16, 24 or 32 bytes), bits 8..15 tlen (tag bytes, 1..16),
note       bits 16..63 ivlen (IV bytes, >= 1). aad is the rest of kia (len kia - klen - ivlen bytes).
note     seal: buf = plaintext || tlen bytes of room; becomes ciphertext || tag.
note     open: buf = ciphertext || tag; on success buf[0..n) becomes the plaintext; on a tag
note     mismatch buf[0..n) is zeroed and 1 is returned. The tag is checked before any plaintext
note     is produced, with an or-accumulated comparison over all tlen bytes.
note     2 (nothing written) when klen is not 16/24/32, tlen is 0 or above 16, ivlen is 0,
note     klen + ivlen > len kia, len buf < tlen, or the data part exceeds 2^36 - 32 bytes
note     ((2^32 - 2) counter blocks, SP 800-38D 5.2.1.1).
note   aead_aes128gcm_seal kn aad buf / aead_aes128gcm_open kn aad buf
note     TLS 1.3 AEAD_AES_128_GCM (RFC 5116 5.1): kn = key(16) || nonce(12), 16-byte tag, the same
note     in-place buffer and return codes as aead_chacha_*; 2 when len kn is not 28 or len buf < 16.
note
note Constant time. AES is bitsliced (BearSSL aes_ct64 layout by T. Pornin, MIT licence: four
note blocks in eight 64-bit planes, plane j holding bit j of every state byte). SubBytes is the
note Boyar-Peralta depth-16 straight-line program for the AES S-box (J. Boyar, R. Peralta, "A small
note depth-16 circuit for the AES S-box", IFIP SEC 2012, LNCS 376, pp. 287-298; eprint 2011/332),
note transcribed from the authors' file https://www.cs.yale.edu/homes/peralta/CircuitStuff/
note AESDEPTH16SIZE125 (125 gates: 34 AND, 91 XOR/XNOR; sha256 b72f635d5a58e06b44d4040b95901da2
note 7418ec5a037f9123392155e96966f162). The key schedule's SubWord uses the same circuit. GHASH is
note the bit-serial multiply of SP 800-38D Algorithm 1 with every conditional replaced by an
note all-ones/all-zeros mask. No array is indexed by key, data, H or any other secret; every
note branch and loop count depends only on lengths, the key size and the tag-check outcome.
note Caveat: omc emits plain AArch64; this relies on LDR/STR/EOR/AND/ORR/shift/ROR/SUB being
note data-independent in time. No DIT bit is set. Secret workspaces (round keys, H, state) are
note zeroed before the entry points return.
note
note Workspace k (ulong AGKN) cells: 0..119 round keys (round r, plane j at 8r + j); 120 number of
note rounds; 121,122 H; 123,124 GHASH accumulator Y; 125,126 E(K, J0); 127,128 J0; 129 next counter
note (32 bits); 130 tag length. 128-bit values are two big-endian halves (hi = bytes 0..7).
note Workspace s (ulong AGSN) cells: 0..7 bit planes; 8..147 S-box gates (gate Ti in cell 7 + i);
note 150..157 the four blocks of aes_enc4 (block b: hi at 150 + 2b, lo at 151 + 2b).

const AGKN ulong 136
const AGSN ulong 160
note GHASH reduction R = 11100001 || 0^120 (SP 800-38D 6.3), high half
const AGR ulong 0xe100000000000000

note 8 x 8 bit transpose of s[0..8) inside every byte position (BearSSL br_aes_ct64_ortho);
note its own inverse
fn aes_ortho s edit ulong AGSN to void
a = ulong 0
b = ulong 0
for i ulong 4 unroll
a = get s mul i 2
b = get s add mul i 2 1
put s mul i 2 or and a 0x5555555555555555 shl and b 0x5555555555555555 1
put s add mul i 2 1 or and shr a 1 0x5555555555555555 and b 0xaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa
end
for i ulong 4 unroll
a = get s add and i 1 mul shr i 1 4
b = get s add add and i 1 mul shr i 1 4 2
put s add and i 1 mul shr i 1 4 or and a 0x3333333333333333 shl and b 0x3333333333333333 2
put s add add and i 1 mul shr i 1 4 2 or and shr a 2 0x3333333333333333 and b 0xcccccccccccccccc
end
for i ulong 4 unroll
a = get s i
b = get s add i 4
put s i or and a 0x0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f shl and b 0x0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f 4
put s add i 4 or and shr a 4 0x0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0f and b 0xf0f0f0f0f0f0f0f0
end
end

note SubBytes on all 64 bytes of the planes: the Boyar-Peralta depth-16 circuit, one gate a line.
note Inputs U0 (most significant bit) .. U7 are planes s[7] .. s[0]; gate Ti is s[7 + i]; outputs
note S0 .. S7 go to s[7] .. s[0]. "+" is xor, "x" is and, "#" (xnor) is not xor. Every input is
note read before the first output is written.
fn aes_sbox s edit ulong AGSN to void
put s 8 xor get s 1 get s 3
put s 9 xor get s 4 get s 7
put s 10 xor get s 6 get s 5
put s 11 xor get s 0 get s 10
put s 12 xor get s 8 get s 9
put s 13 xor get s 6 get s 2
put s 14 xor get s 7 get s 1
put s 15 xor get s 8 get s 13
put s 16 xor get s 1 get s 11
put s 17 xor get s 4 get s 11
put s 18 xor get s 0 get s 12
put s 19 xor get s 12 get s 13
put s 20 xor get s 5 get s 2
put s 21 xor get s 10 get s 12
put s 22 xor get s 2 get s 14
put s 23 xor get s 7 get s 2
put s 24 xor get s 0 get s 15
put s 25 xor get s 1 get s 2
put s 26 xor get s 9 get s 25
put s 27 xor get s 11 get s 22
put s 28 xor get s 8 get s 20
put s 29 xor get s 7 get s 11
put s 46 xor get s 28 get s 12
put s 47 xor get s 28 get s 14
put s 48 xor get s 14 get s 26
put s 49 xor get s 23 get s 21
put s 50 xor get s 29 get s 24
put s 51 and get s 26 get s 12
put s 52 and get s 27 get s 18
put s 53 xor get s 19 get s 51
put s 54 and get s 17 get s 0
put s 55 xor get s 54 get s 51
put s 56 and get s 14 get s 28
put s 57 and get s 16 get s 11
put s 58 xor get s 47 get s 56
put s 59 and get s 29 get s 24
put s 60 xor get s 59 get s 56
put s 61 and get s 9 get s 15
put s 62 and get s 48 get s 46
put s 63 xor get s 62 get s 61
put s 64 and get s 23 get s 21
put s 65 xor get s 64 get s 61
put s 66 xor get s 53 get s 52
put s 67 xor get s 55 get s 49
put s 68 xor get s 58 get s 57
put s 69 xor get s 60 get s 65
put s 70 xor get s 66 get s 63
put s 71 xor get s 67 get s 65
put s 72 xor get s 68 get s 63
put s 73 xor get s 69 get s 50
put s 74 xor get s 72 get s 73
put s 75 and get s 72 get s 70
put s 76 xor get s 71 get s 75
put s 77 xor get s 70 get s 71
put s 78 xor get s 73 get s 75
put s 79 and get s 78 get s 77
put s 80 and get s 76 get s 74
put s 81 and get s 70 get s 73
put s 82 and get s 77 get s 81
put s 83 xor get s 77 get s 75
put s 84 and get s 71 get s 72
put s 85 and get s 74 get s 84
put s 86 xor get s 74 get s 75
put s 87 xor get s 71 get s 79
put s 88 xor get s 82 get s 83
put s 89 xor get s 73 get s 80
put s 90 xor get s 85 get s 86
put s 91 xor get s 88 get s 90
put s 92 xor get s 87 get s 89
put s 93 xor get s 87 get s 88
put s 94 xor get s 89 get s 90
put s 95 xor get s 92 get s 91
put s 96 and get s 94 get s 12
put s 97 and get s 90 get s 18
put s 98 and get s 89 get s 0
put s 99 and get s 93 get s 28
put s 100 and get s 88 get s 11
put s 101 and get s 87 get s 24
put s 102 and get s 92 get s 15
put s 103 and get s 95 get s 46
put s 104 and get s 91 get s 21
put s 105 and get s 94 get s 26
put s 106 and get s 90 get s 27
put s 107 and get s 89 get s 17
put s 108 and get s 93 get s 14
put s 109 and get s 88 get s 16
put s 110 and get s 87 get s 29
put s 111 and get s 92 get s 9
put s 112 and get s 95 get s 48
put s 113 and get s 91 get s 23
put s 114 xor get s 111 get s 112
put s 115 xor get s 100 get s 106
put s 116 xor get s 103 get s 114
put s 117 xor get s 105 get s 115
put s 118 xor get s 98 get s 108
put s 119 xor get s 96 get s 99
put s 120 xor get s 114 get s 119
put s 121 xor get s 97 get s 117
put s 122 xor get s 96 get s 102
put s 123 xor get s 101 get s 109
put s 124 xor get s 104 get s 110
put s 125 xor get s 98 get s 121
put s 126 xor get s 118 get s 124
put s 127 xor get s 107 get s 115
put s 128 xor get s 99 get s 102
put s 129 xor get s 117 get s 128
put s 130 xor get s 113 get s 126
put s 131 xor get s 111 get s 122
put s 132 xor get s 118 get s 123
put s 7 xor get s 116 get s 129
put s 5 not xor get s 130 get s 131
put s 135 xor get s 101 get s 114
put s 4 xor get s 120 get s 121
put s 3 xor get s 125 get s 135
put s 138 xor get s 100 get s 108
put s 139 xor get s 119 get s 127
put s 0 not xor get s 120 get s 132
put s 141 xor get s 104 get s 123
put s 142 xor get s 138 get s 141
put s 143 xor get s 100 get s 122
put s 1 not xor get s 116 get s 142
put s 145 xor get s 126 get s 139
put s 2 xor get s 116 get s 145
put s 147 xor get s 121 get s 143
put s 6 not xor get s 116 get s 147
end

note ShiftRows: row r of every plane is the 16 bits at 16r (column c at 16r + 4c, block in the low
note two bits); row r rotates left by r columns
fn aes_shrows s edit ulong AGSN to void
x = ulong 0
y = ulong 0
for j ulong 8 unroll
x = get s j
y = and x 0xffff
y = or y shr and x 0xfff00000 4
y = or y shl and x 0xf0000 12
y = or y shr and x 0xff0000000000 8
y = or y shl and x 0xff00000000 8
y = or y shr and x 0xf000000000000000 12
y = or y shl and x 0xfff000000000000 4
put s j y
end
end

note MixColumns: with r = q rotated right 16 (the next row) and u = q xor r, out = xtime(u) xor r
note xor rotr32(u); xtime moves plane 7 into planes 0, 1, 3, 4. u goes to s[8..16).
fn aes_mixcol s edit ulong AGSN to void
x = ulong 0
for j ulong 8 unroll
x = get s j
put s add 8 j xor x rotr x 16
end
put s 0 xor xor get s 15 rotr get s 0 16 rotr get s 8 32
put s 1 xor xor xor get s 8 get s 15 rotr get s 1 16 rotr get s 9 32
put s 2 xor xor get s 9 rotr get s 2 16 rotr get s 10 32
put s 3 xor xor xor get s 10 get s 15 rotr get s 3 16 rotr get s 11 32
put s 4 xor xor xor get s 11 get s 15 rotr get s 4 16 rotr get s 12 32
put s 5 xor xor get s 12 rotr get s 5 16 rotr get s 13 32
put s 6 xor xor get s 13 rotr get s 6 16 rotr get s 14 32
put s 7 xor xor get s 14 rotr get s 7 16 rotr get s 15 32
end

note AddRoundKey with round r
fn aes_ark k view ulong AGKN s edit ulong AGSN r ulong to void
o = shl r 3
for j ulong 8 unroll
put s j xor get s j get k add o j
end
end

note bytes 0..3 of x to bytes 0, 2, 4, 6 (br_aes_ct64_interleave_in)
fn aes_spread x ulong to ulong inline
y = and or x shl x 16 0x0000ffff0000ffff
ret and or y shl y 8 0x00ff00ff00ff00ff
end

note the inverse of aes_spread on bytes 0, 2, 4, 6 of x
fn aes_unspr x ulong to ulong inline
y = and x 0x00ff00ff00ff00ff
y = and or y shr y 8 0x0000ffff0000ffff
ret and or y shr y 16 0xffffffff
end

fn aes_bswap x ulong to ulong
y = or and shr x 8 0x00ff00ff00ff00ff shl and x 0x00ff00ff00ff00ff 8
y = or and shr y 16 0x0000ffff0000ffff shl and y 0x0000ffff0000ffff 16
ret rotr y 32
end

note the four big-endian blocks s[150..158) into bit planes s[0..8): block b's little-endian words
note w0..w3 give s[b] = spread(w0) | spread(w2) << 8 and s[b + 4] = spread(w1) | spread(w3) << 8
fn aes_inblk s edit ulong AGSN to void
x = ulong 0
y = ulong 0
for b ulong 4 unroll
x = aes_bswap get s add 150 mul b 2
y = aes_bswap get s add 151 mul b 2
put s b or aes_spread and x 0xffffffff shl aes_spread and y 0xffffffff 8
put s add b 4 or aes_spread shr x 32 shl aes_spread shr y 32 8
end
aes_ortho s
end

note bit planes s[0..8) back to the four big-endian blocks s[150..158)
fn aes_outblk s edit ulong AGSN to void
aes_ortho s
x = ulong 0
y = ulong 0
for b ulong 4 unroll
x = get s b
y = get s add b 4
put s add 150 mul b 2 aes_bswap or aes_unspr x shl aes_unspr y 32
put s add 151 mul b 2 aes_bswap or aes_unspr shr x 8 shl aes_unspr shr y 8 32
end
end

note encrypt the four blocks s[150..158) in place with the round keys in k
fn aes_enc4 k view ulong AGKN s edit ulong AGSN to void
aes_inblk s
nr = get k 120
aes_ark k s 0
for r ulong sub nr 1
aes_sbox s
aes_shrows s
aes_mixcol s
aes_ark k s add r 1
end
aes_sbox s
aes_shrows s
aes_ark k s nr
aes_outblk s
end

note SubWord of the 32-bit little-endian word x through the bitsliced S-box
fn aes_subw s edit ulong AGSN x ulong to ulong
for j ulong 8 unroll
put s j 0
end
put s 0 x
aes_ortho s
aes_sbox s
aes_ortho s
ret and get s 0 0xffffffff
end

note FIPS 197 5.2 key expansion of w[0 .. nk) into w[nk .. 4 (nk + 7)); words are little-endian as
note loaded from the key bytes, so RotWord is a right rotation by 8 and Rcon is in the low byte.
note The branches depend on the word index and the key size only.
fn aes_expand w edit ulong 60 s edit ulong AGSN nk ulong to void
rc = ulong 1
j = ulong 0
t = get w sub nk 1
for c ulong sub shl add nk 7 2 nk
if eq j 0
t = xor aes_subw s or shr t 8 and shl t 24 0xff000000 rc
rc = shl rc 1
if gt rc 255
rc = xor rc 0x11b
end
else
if gt nk 6
if eq j 4
t = aes_subw s t
end
end
end
t = xor t get w c
put w add c nk t
j = add j 1
if eq j nk
j = 0
end
end
end

note the key schedule into k: number of rounds, then each round key as bit planes in
note k[8r .. 8r + 8). len key is 16, 24 or 32 (checked by the caller).
fn aes_setkey k edit ulong AGKN s edit ulong AGSN key view uchar * to void
w = new ulong 60 0
nk = shr len key 2
nr = add nk 6
put k 120 nr
x = ulong 0
q = ulong 0
for i ulong nk
q = shl i 2
x = or ulong get key q shl ulong get key add q 1 8
x = or x shl ulong get key add q 2 16
put w i or x shl ulong get key add q 3 24
end
aes_expand w s nk
aes_rkeys k s w
for i ulong 60
put w i 0
end
end

note round key r (words w[4r .. 4r + 4)) as bit planes in k[8r .. 8r + 8): the same block in all
note four lanes, through aes_inblk
fn aes_rkeys k edit ulong AGKN s edit ulong AGSN w view ulong 60 to void
q = ulong 0
x = ulong 0
for r ulong add get k 120 1
q = shl r 2
x = or get w q shl get w add q 1 32
put s 150 aes_bswap x
x = or get w add q 2 shl get w add q 3 32
put s 151 aes_bswap x
for b ulong 3 unroll
put s add 152 mul b 2 get s 150
put s add 153 mul b 2 get s 151
end
aes_inblk s
for i ulong 8 unroll
put k add shl r 3 i get s i
end
end
end

note Y = Y * H in GF(2^128) (SP 800-38D 6.3 Algorithm 1): Z ^= V where bit i of Y is set,
note V = V >> 1, xor R where V's last bit was set; both conditions are masks
fn gcm_mul k edit ulong AGKN to void
x = get k 123
vh = get k 121
vl = get k 122
zh = ulong 0
zl = ulong 0
m = ulong 0
for i ulong 64 unroll
m = sub 0 and shr x sub 63 i 1
zh = xor zh and vh m
zl = xor zl and vl m
m = sub 0 and vl 1
vl = or shr vl 1 shl vh 63
vh = xor shr vh 1 and m AGR
end
x = get k 124
for i ulong 64 unroll
m = sub 0 and shr x sub 63 i 1
zh = xor zh and vh m
zl = xor zl and vl m
m = sub 0 and vl 1
vl = or shr vl 1 shl vh 63
vh = xor shr vh 1 and m AGR
end
put k 123 zh
put k 124 zl
end

note absorb the 16 bytes of d at o into Y
fn gcm_ablk k edit ulong AGKN d view uchar * o ulong to void
h = ulong 0
l = ulong 0
for i ulong 8 unroll
h = or shl h 8 ulong get d add o i
l = or shl l 8 ulong get d add o add i 8
end
put k 123 xor get k 123 h
put k 124 xor get k 124 l
gcm_mul k
end

note the whole blocks of d (fewer than 2^20)
fn gcm_absrun k edit ulong AGKN d view uchar * to void
for i ulong shr len d 4
gcm_ablk k d shl i 4
end
end

note GHASH update with d, the last partial block padded with zeros (runs of 8 MiB keep every
note rolled loop under its 1000000 passes)
fn gcm_absorb k edit ulong AGKN d view uchar * to void
p = new uchar 16 0
n = len d
q = ulong 0
for a ulong shr n 23
gcm_absrun k part d q 0x800000
q = add q 0x800000
end
m = sub n and n 15
gcm_absrun k part d q sub m q
r = sub n m
if gt r 0
for i ulong r
put p i get d add m i
end
gcm_ablk k p 0
end
end

note the length block [8a]_64 || [8c]_64
fn gcm_lens k edit ulong AGKN a ulong c ulong to void
put k 123 xor get k 123 shl a 3
put k 124 xor get k 124 shl c 3
gcm_mul k
end

note the next four counter blocks J0[0..12) || inc32 into s[150..158)
fn gcm_cblk k edit ulong AGKN s edit ulong AGSN to void
c = get k 129
h = get k 127
l = and get k 128 0xffffffff00000000
for b ulong 4 unroll
put s add 150 mul b 2 h
put s add 151 mul b 2 or l and add c b 0xffffffff
end
put k 129 and add c 4 0xffffffff
end

note d[o .. o + 64) ^= the 64 key stream bytes in s[150..158)
fn gcm_xor64 s view ulong AGSN d edit uchar * o ulong to void
x = ulong 0
q = ulong 0
for w ulong 8 unroll
x = get s add 150 w
for p ulong 8 unroll
q = add o add shl w 3 p
put d q xor get d q uchar and shr x sub 56 shl p 3 0xff
end
end
end

note GCTR over d from the stored counter (len d below 2^25 + 64)
fn gcm_ctrrun k edit ulong AGKN s edit ulong AGSN d edit uchar * to void
n = len d
for j ulong shr n 6
gcm_cblk k s
aes_enc4 k s
gcm_xor64 s d shl j 6
end
r = and n 63
if gt r 0
gcm_cblk k s
aes_enc4 k s
gcm_xorn s part d sub n r r
end
end

note d[0 .. len d) ^= the first len d (below 64) key stream bytes in s[150..158)
fn gcm_xorn s view ulong AGSN d edit uchar * to void
x = ulong 0
z = ulong 0
for i ulong len d
x = get s add 150 shr i 3
z = sub 56 shl and i 7 3
put d i xor get d i uchar and shr x z 0xff
end
end

fn gcm_ctr k edit ulong AGKN s edit ulong AGSN d edit uchar * to void
n = len d
q = ulong 0
for a ulong shr n 25
gcm_ctrrun k s part d q 0x2000000
q = add q 0x2000000
end
gcm_ctrrun k s part d q sub n q
end

note key schedule, H = E(K, 0^128), J0 (SP 800-38D 7.1 step 2), E(K, J0) and the first counter.
note key = kia[0 .. kl), iv = kia[kl .. kl + il).
fn gcm_init k edit ulong AGKN s edit ulong AGSN kia view uchar * kl ulong il ulong to void
aes_setkey k s part kia 0 kl
h = ulong 0
l = ulong 1
if eq il 12
for i ulong 8 unroll
h = or shl h 8 ulong get kia add kl i
end
l = ulong 0
for i ulong 4 unroll
l = or shl l 8 ulong get kia add add kl 8 i
end
l = or shl l 32 1
end
for i ulong 8 unroll
put s add 150 i 0
end
put s 152 h
put s 153 l
aes_enc4 k s
put k 121 get s 150
put k 122 get s 151
put k 125 get s 152
put k 126 get s 153
if ne il 12
put k 123 0
put k 124 0
gcm_absorb k part kia kl il
gcm_lens k 0 il
h = get k 123
l = get k 124
put s 150 h
put s 151 l
aes_enc4 k s
put k 125 get s 150
put k 126 get s 151
end
put k 123 0
put k 124 0
put k 127 h
put k 128 l
put k 129 and add l 1 0xffffffff
end

note the tag Y ^ E(K, J0) into k[123], k[124] after the length block of a aad bytes and c data bytes
fn gcm_tag k edit ulong AGKN a ulong c ulong to void
gcm_lens k a c
put k 123 xor get k 123 get k 125
put k 124 xor get k 124 get k 126
end

note byte i (0..15) of the tag in k[123], k[124]
fn gcm_tbyte k view ulong AGKN i ulong to uchar
x = get k 123
if ge i 8
x = get k 124
end
z = sub 56 shl and i 7 3
ret uchar and shr x z 0xff
end

fn gcm_seal1 k edit ulong AGKN s edit ulong AGSN aad view uchar * buf edit uchar * to void
t = get k 130
n = sub len buf t
gcm_ctr k s part buf 0 n
gcm_absorb k aad
gcm_absorb k view part buf 0 n
gcm_tag k len aad n
for i ulong t
put buf add n i gcm_tbyte k i
end
end

fn gcm_open1 k edit ulong AGKN s edit ulong AGSN aad view uchar * buf edit uchar * to ulong
t = get k 130
n = sub len buf t
gcm_absorb k aad
gcm_absorb k view part buf 0 n
gcm_tag k len aad n
d = uchar 0
for i ulong t
d = or d xor get buf add n i gcm_tbyte k i
end
if ne d 0
gcm_wipe part buf 0 n
ret 1
end
gcm_ctr k s part buf 0 n
ret 0
end

note zero d, any length (two loop levels keep each under 1000000 passes)
fn gcm_wipe d edit uchar * to void
n = len d
for a ulong shr n 19
for b ulong 0x80000
put d add shl a 19 b 0
end
end
m = and n 0x7ffff
o = sub n m
for b ulong m
put d add o b 0
end
end

fn gcm_clear k edit ulong AGKN s edit ulong AGSN to void
for i ulong AGKN
put k i 0
end
for i ulong AGSN
put s i 0
end
end

note 0 when ctl and the lengths are acceptable (see the API note), else 2
fn gcm_chk ctl ulong ka ulong bl ulong to ulong
kl = and ctl 0xff
tl = and shr ctl 8 0xff
il = shr ctl 16
ok = ulong 0
if eq kl 16
ok = 1
end
if eq kl 24
ok = 1
end
if eq kl 32
ok = 1
end
if eq ok 0
ret 2
end
if eq tl 0
ret 2
end
if gt tl 16
ret 2
end
if eq il 0
ret 2
end
if gt kl ka
ret 2
end
if gt il sub ka kl
ret 2
end
if gt tl bl
ret 2
end
if gt sub bl tl 0xfffffffe0
ret 2
end
ret 0
end

fn aes_gcm_seal ctl ulong kia view uchar * buf edit uchar * to ulong
k = new ulong AGKN 0
s = new ulong AGSN 0
if ne gcm_chk ctl len kia len buf 0
ret 2
end
kl = and ctl 0xff
il = shr ctl 16
put k 130 and shr ctl 8 0xff
gcm_init k s kia kl il
q = add kl il
gcm_seal1 k s part kia q sub len kia q buf
gcm_clear k s
ret 0
end

fn aes_gcm_open ctl ulong kia view uchar * buf edit uchar * to ulong
k = new ulong AGKN 0
s = new ulong AGSN 0
if ne gcm_chk ctl len kia len buf 0
ret 2
end
kl = and ctl 0xff
il = shr ctl 16
put k 130 and shr ctl 8 0xff
gcm_init k s kia kl il
q = add kl il
r = gcm_open1 k s part kia q sub len kia q buf
gcm_clear k s
ret r
end

note TLS 1.3 AEAD_AES_128_GCM: kn = key(16) || nonce(12), 16-byte tag
fn aead_aes128gcm_seal kn view uchar * aad view uchar * buf edit uchar * to ulong
k = new ulong AGKN 0
s = new ulong AGSN 0
if ne gcm_chk 0xc1010 28 len buf 0
ret 2
end
if ne len kn 28
ret 2
end
put k 130 16
gcm_init k s kn 16 12
gcm_seal1 k s aad buf
gcm_clear k s
ret 0
end

fn aead_aes128gcm_open kn view uchar * aad view uchar * buf edit uchar * to ulong
k = new ulong AGKN 0
s = new ulong AGSN 0
if ne gcm_chk 0xc1010 28 len buf 0
ret 2
end
if ne len kn 28
ret 2
end
put k 130 16
gcm_init k s kn 16 12
r = gcm_open1 k s aad buf
gcm_clear k s
ret r
end
